      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Fourier Transform still works perfectly on noise, but the result tells you something important: random, unstructured noise tends to spread its energy across a very wide range of frequencies. Essentially, a lot of random noise shows up as a high, relatively constant energy level across the entire frequency spectrum. Therefore, while the transform doesn't eliminate the noise, it makes the noise's presence obvious as broad frequency energy.",
